[agent:result] ) -> 'tuple[Job | None, great_expectations.core.ExpectationSuiteValidationResult | None]' method of hsfs.feature_group.FeatureGroup instance
[agent:result]     Persist the metadata and materialize the feature group to the feature store.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Warning: Changed in 3.3.0
[agent:result]         `insert` and `save` methods are now async by default in non-spark clients.
[agent:result]         To achieve the old behaviour, set `wait` argument to `True`.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Calling `save` creates the metadata for the feature group in the feature store.
[agent:result]     If a Pandas DataFrame, Polars DatFrame, RDD or Ndarray is provided, the data is written to the online/offline feature store as specified.
[agent:result]     By default, this writes the feature group to the offline storage, and if `online_enabled` for the feature group, also to the online feature store.
[agent:result]     The `features` dataframe can be a Spark DataFrame or RDD, a Pandas DataFrame, or a two-dimensional Numpy array or a two-dimensional Python nested list.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]     Parameters:
[agent:result]         features:
[agent:result]             Features to be saved.
[agent:result]             This argument is optional if the feature list is provided in the `create_feature_group` or in the `get_or_create_feature_group` method invokation.
[agent:result]         write_options:
[agent:result]             Additional write options as key-value pairs.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             When using the `python` engine, write_options can contain the following entries:
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]             - key `spark` and value an object of type [hsfs.core.job_configuration.JobConfiguration][hsfs.core.job_configuration.JobConfiguration] to configure the Hopsworks Job used to write data into the feature group.
[agent:result]             - key `wait_for_job` and value `True` or `False` to configure whether or not to the save call should return only after the Hopsworks Job has finished.
[agent:result]               By default it does not wait.
[agent:result]             - key `wait_for_online_ingestion` and value `True` or `False` to configure whether or not to the save call should return only after the Hopsworks online ingestion has finished.
[agent:result]               By default it does not wait.
[agent:result]             - key `online_ingestion_options` and value a dict to configure online ingestion behaviour.
[agent:result]               Supported keys:
[agent:result]                 - `timeout`: seconds to wait for online ingestion completion, default `60`, set to `0` for indefinite.
[agent:result]                   Applies only when `wait_for_online_ingestion` is `True` or the `wait` parameter is `True`.
[agent:result]                 - `period`: polling interval in seconds, default `1`.
[agent:result]                   Applies only when `wait_for_online_ingestion` is `True` or the `wait` parameter is `True`.
[agent:result]                 - `upsert_if_newer`: `True` or `False` to only update a row if the new value is newer than the existing one, defaults to `False`.
[agent:result]                 - `mark_online_rows`: `True` or `False` to filter rows for online ingestion based on event time and primary key deduplication, defaults to `True`.
[agent:result]                 - `disable_online_ingestion_count`: `True` or `False` to disable sending the total number of entries to the online ingestion tracking system, defaults to `False`.
[agent:result]                   When `True`, no batch size is known to the ingestion tracker so `wait_for_online_ingestion` will wait until `timeout` is reached.
[agent:result]             - key `start_offline_backfill` and value `True` or `False` to configure whether or not to start the materialization job to write data to the offline storage. `start_offline_backfill` is deprecated.
[agent:result]               Use `start_offline_materialization` instead.
[agent:result]             - key `start_offline_materialization` and value `True` or `False` to configure whether or not to start the materialization job to write data to the offline storage.
[agent:result]               By default the materialization job gets started immediately.
[agent:result]             - key `kafka_producer_config` and value an object of type [properties](https://docs.confluent.io/platform/current/clients/librdkafka/html/md_CONFIGURATION.htmln) used to configure the Kafka client.
[agent:result]               To optimize for throughput in high latency connection, consider changing the [producer properties](https://docs.confluent.io/cloud/current/client-apps/optimizing/throughput.html#producer).
[agent:result]             - key `internal_kafka` and value `True` or `False` in case you established connectivity from you Python environment to the internal advertised listeners of the Hopsworks Kafka Cluster.
[agent:result]               Defaults to `False` and will use external listeners when connecting from outside of Hopsworks.
[agent:result]             - key `delta.enableChangeDataFeed` set to a *string* value of true or false to enable or disable cdf operations on the feature group delta table.
[agent:result]               Set to true by default on Feature Group creation.
[agent:result] 
